WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.480
What happened to Josh Holloway after the whirlwind
success of Lost came to an end?

00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:10.140
What does an actor who once struggled to book
guest roles do after the gleam of his big

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:11.120
break wears off?

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:13.300
We've got the whole story for you right here.

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:19.180
Holloway was born in 1969 in San Jose, California,
the second of four brothers.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:23.760
When he was two, he moved with his family
into a trailer in Georgia's Blue Ridge Mountains.

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:28.619
His acting career got a huge break in 1993
in the form of the Aerosmith music video for

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:32.620
"Cryin,'" when he played a thief who tries
to snatch Alicia Silverstone's purse.

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:36.760
He eventually started grabbing TV guest roles
on shows like Angel and CSI.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:42.650
His most significant pre-Lost project was
perhaps the 2002 Sci-Fi original movie Sabretooth,

00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:45.700
in which he fights to survive the rampage
of a prehistoric cat.

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:50.100
But he was struggling so much that he almost
quit acting to become a realtor in 2004.

00:00:50.110 --> 00:00:53.570
Later that year, though, his career really
took off into the stratosphere.

00:00:53.570 --> 00:00:58.290
In TV's streaming age, it's hard to convey
just how big a deal Lost was in its heyday.

00:00:58.290 --> 00:01:03.280
Averaging over 15 million viewers a week during
its first season, it inspired the sort of

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:07.370
obsessive fan culture that makes even Game
of Thrones viewers blush.

00:01:07.370 --> 00:01:12.409
In the modern media era where nerd culture
reigns supreme, it might be difficult to appreciate

00:01:12.409 --> 00:01:15.220
how uniquely dedicated Lost's fanbase was.

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:21.440
As loveable rogue James "Sawyer" Ford, Holloway
instantly shot into stardom in a way he probably

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:22.840
never imagined possible.

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:28.320
"You sure know how to make a girl feel special,
Sawyer."

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:29.820
"You're incredible, Sawyer."

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:35.000
One might think becoming a household name
overnight would do wonders for Holloway's

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:38.680
acting career, but that actually wasn't the
case, at least not at first.

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:44.600
During Lost's 2004 to 2010 run, the only outside
projects he worked on were just a few low-budget

00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:45.100
films.

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:48.820
It isn't hard to see why this was the case,
as he and his family spent most of the year

00:01:48.820 --> 00:01:51.260
in Hawaii while he was shooting the the ABC
series.

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:55.700
Holloway also had to turn down some major
roles because of his grueling shooting schedule,

00:01:55.900 --> 00:01:58.979
perhaps most notably the part of Gambit in
the X-Men films.

00:01:58.979 --> 00:02:02.869
Even after Lost ended, it seemed as if bad
luck would curse Holloway into becoming a

00:02:02.869 --> 00:02:04.040
has-been pretty quickly.

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:08.039
At one point he was considered for the part
of Crossbones in Captain America: The Winter

00:02:08.039 --> 00:02:12.239
Soldier, and he even turned down the CBS series
Person of Interest because he didn't want

00:02:12.239 --> 00:02:14.090
to move his family across the country.

00:02:14.090 --> 00:02:17.180
He would eventually work his way into more
acting opportunities, but it's hard to look

00:02:17.180 --> 00:02:20.819
past what could've been if a couple of these
chances had broken in his favor.

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:24.380
"I was thinking about Lost today and how much
I miss it and I’m sure you’re sick of

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:25.500
it with that stuff"

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:29.280
“I’m not because my wife tells me that
often.”

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:30.000
"She does?"

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:30.500
"She does."

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:34.680
After struggling to get a serious film career
off the ground in the immediate years after

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:40.250
Lost, Holloway returned to the small screen
in 2014 as the main character in the CBS series

00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:40.760
Intelligence.

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:45.000
The show was a cyber-themed action-adventure
thriller that unfortunately for Holloway only

00:02:45.019 --> 00:02:47.629
aired 13 episodes before getting the axe.

00:02:47.629 --> 00:02:52.150
He starred as Gabriel, a tech-enhanced man
designed to tackle major threats while working

00:02:52.150 --> 00:02:53.520
for U.S. Cyber Command.

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:58.459
With Intelligence, CBS wasn't trying to reinvent
the wheel, and there's something to be said

00:02:58.459 --> 00:03:03.340
for easy-to-digest thrillers where the good
guys are Capital-G Good and the bad guys are

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:04.440
shady beyond belief.

00:03:05.010 --> 00:03:10.080
Alas, it never lived up to the network's expectations,
nor was it ever given a full chance to find

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:11.080
a real audience.

00:03:11.880 --> 00:03:17.200
Holloway eventually found another winning
project in 2016 in the form of Colony, a sci-fi

00:03:17.201 --> 00:03:20.030
drama that ran on USA Network for three seasons.

00:03:20.030 --> 00:03:24.451
Though it never managed to capture a significantly
large audience, it was a cult hit that was

00:03:24.460 --> 00:03:26.120
generally well-regarded by critics.

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:30.640
It even managed to garner three straight Saturn
Award nominations for Best Science Fiction

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:31.640
Television Series.

00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:36.360
Colony was set in a dystopian version of Los
Angeles, where residents live under military

00:03:36.370 --> 00:03:40.700
occupation by the Transitional Authority,
an organization serving an extraterrestrial

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:42.280
group referred to as the "Hosts."

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:47.260
Holloway starred as a former U.S. Army Ranger
and FBI Special Agent who was trying to save

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:48.260
his missing son.

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:50.080
"How do you live with this job?"

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:55.080
Coming off the heels of Colony, Holloway landed
a role in the upcoming third season of Paramount

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:56.240
Network's Yellowstone.

00:03:56.290 --> 00:04:00.480
The show stars Kevin Coster as billionaire
John Dutton, the patriarch of a family that

00:04:00.489 --> 00:04:03.269
controls the largest contiguous ranch in the
United States.

00:04:03.269 --> 00:04:07.959
The Duttons are under constant attack by those
around them, and show co-creator Taylor Sheridan

00:04:07.959 --> 00:04:12.400
wants the show to be a look at a violent world
separated from typical media scrutiny.

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:13.530
Sheridan has said,

00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:15.780
"The show is both timely and timeless.

00:04:15.909 --> 00:04:20.500
As much as it explores themes painfully relevant
to the world today, it explores the very essence

00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:24.270
of family, and how the actions of one member
can alter the course of generations."

00:04:24.270 --> 00:04:29.090
Holloway has signed on for a season-long arc
as a charming hedge fund manager with ambitious

00:04:29.090 --> 00:04:30.120
plans in Montana.

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:34.280
With a string of regular TV roles over the
last several years, it's safe to say that

00:04:34.280 --> 00:04:36.720
the future is now looking bright for Josh
Holloway.

